From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot automatically from eMMC only

The vendor BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES order is USB, SD, NVMe x2, SCSI, eMMC, MTD,
RKNAND, PXE, DHCP, so eMMC is the fifth target the distro boot framework
tries. Every normal eMMC boot therefore runs "usb start", probes the SD
slot, and runs "pci enum" plus "nvme scan" first. On this SoC family the
PCIe link training alone costs about 720ms when no endpoint answers and
over 1.2s when one does, because rk_pcie_link_up() waits 200ms for
T_PVPERL, retries for 500ms, and then sleeps a further 1000ms once the
link is up.

Mixtile products boot from eMMC, so make eMMC the only automatic boot
target. This only trims the generated boot_targets and bootcmd_<target>
list: BOOTENV_SHARED_MMC, _PCI, _USB, _SCSI and _NVME are emitted from
their own CONFIG_* symbols, so mmc_boot, usb_boot, nvme_boot, nvme_init
and boot_pci_enum all remain in the environment, and the mmc, usb, pci
and nvme commands are untouched. Everything stays available from the
U-Boot prompt; it just no longer runs unattended.

diff --git a/include/configs/rockchip-common.h b/include/configs/rockchip-common.h
index e1c4779b..dd6839c3 100644
--- a/include/configs/rockchip-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/rockchip-common.h
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_references_MTD_without_CONFIG_CMD_MTD_BLK
 #endif
 
-/* First try to boot from SD (index 1), then NVME (if CMD_NVME is enabled), then SCSI (if CMD_SCSI is enabled),then eMMC (index 0) */
+/* Mixtile: eMMC (index 0) is the only automatic boot target */
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(CMD_MMC)
 	#define BOOT_TARGET_EMMC(func)	func(MMC, mmc, 0)
 	#define BOOT_TARGET_SD(func)	func(MMC, mmc, 1)
@@ -119,15 +119,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_USB(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_SD(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_NVME(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_SCSI(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_EMMC(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_MTD(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_RKNAND(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_PXE(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DHCP(func)
+	BOOT_TARGET_EMMC(func)
 
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
